13:["$","section",null,{"className":"reference-section battle-flow-section","id":"battle-flow","children":["$","$L1b",null,{"guide":{"date":"April 6, 1862, about 5–10 a.m.","place":"Shiloh Church, Ray Field, the farm lane through the United States center, Bell Field, and the Hamburg–Savannah Road, Tennessee","result":"Prentiss re-formed part of his routed division, and the divisions of W. H. L. Wallace and Stephen Hurlbut extended the new United States center. Johnston diverted Chalmers and Jackson toward Stuart’s isolated brigade after mistaking it for a full division. On the United States right, Sherman recovered from the initial surprise and held near Shiloh Church for more than two hours. By about 10 a.m., seven Confederate brigades had converged on Sherman and Julius Raith, and Hildebrand’s brigade began to break","facts":[{"label":"New United States center","value":"Nearly one mile from the Corinth Road to the Hamburg–Savannah Road"},{"label":"Prentiss’s reinforcement","value":"About 1,000 fresh men of the 23rd Missouri"},{"label":"Center formed","value":"About 9–9:30 a.m."},{"label":"Stuart’s detached brigade","value":"One Illinois and two Ohio regiments near the river"},{"label":"Gap beside Stuart","value":"About 200 yards, obstructed by woods and a ravine"},{"label":"Cleburne’s formation","value":"Six regiments in one line, roughly one mile wide before terrain divided it"},{"label":"Confederate concentration","value":"Seven brigades against Sherman and Raith by about 9:30 a.m."},{"label":"Sherman’s wound","value":"Buckshot through the right hand; he remained in command"}],"maps":[{"title":"Shiloh battlefield today","caption":"The NPS map identifies Shiloh Church, Ray Field, Bell Field, the Hamburg–Savannah Road, Pittsburg Landing, and the creeks that bounded the battlefield.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shil/planyourvisit/maps.htm","image":"/images/shiloh-nps-auto-tour-map.jpg","alt":"National Park Service map of the Shiloh battlefield"},{"title":"United States positions and Confederate attacks, 9–10 a.m.","caption":"Wallace, Prentiss, and Hurlbut formed a new center while Stuart remained isolated near the river. Seven Confederate brigades converged against Sherman and Raith around Shiloh Church; Chalmers and Jackson were diverted toward Stuart.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shil/learn/historyculture/shiloh-history.htm","image":"/images/shiloh-april-6-midmorning.svg","alt":"Tactical map of the Shiloh battlefield at mid-morning on April 6, 1862"},{"title":"Historical troop-position map","caption":"The 1862 map approved by Beauregard shows the camps, roads, fields, and army positions across the battlefield.","source":"https://www.loc.gov/item/85690890/","image":"/images/shiloh-beauregard-map.jpg","alt":"1862 manuscript map of the Battle of Shiloh"}],"moments":[{"time":"1:10","audioTime":70,"title":"The episode resumes after Prentiss’s defeat","detail":"The Confederate attack had driven Prentiss’s division from its camps, but it had not cut the United States army off from Pittsburg Landing."},{"time":"3:40","audioTime":220,"title":"Confederate troops stopped in the captured camps","detail":"Some formations became disorganized while soldiers searched the tents and collected food and equipment."},{"time":"4:34","audioTime":274,"title":"Johnston received an incorrect report about Stuart","detail":"A cavalry patrol saw Stuart’s detached brigade and reported a United States division moving south near the river."},{"time":"7:02","audioTime":422,"title":"Johnston diverted two brigades","detail":"He sent James Chalmers and John K. Jackson toward Stuart, leaving only one brigade to cover a large part of the Confederate center."},{"time":"8:16","audioTime":496,"title":"Two reserve brigades were redirected","detail":"Johnston changed earlier orders and sent two of Breckinridge’s brigades back toward the right to reinforce the weakened center."},{"time":"8:46","audioTime":526,"title":"Prentiss rebuilt part of his division","detail":"Survivors rallied along a farm lane about 1,200 yards north of their captured camps instead of counterattacking."},{"time":"10:10","audioTime":610,"title":"The 23rd Missouri joined Prentiss","detail":"The newly arrived regiment contributed about 1,000 fresh soldiers, probably more men than Prentiss had rallied from his original division."},{"time":"11:06","audioTime":666,"title":"Wallace and Hurlbut formed a new center","detail":"Their divisions took positions on either side of Prentiss between about 9 and 9:30 a.m."},{"time":"12:16","audioTime":736,"title":"MacArthur extended Hurlbut’s left","detail":"W. H. L. Wallace sent John McArthur’s brigade across the line, but a 200-yard wooded gap still separated it from Stuart."},{"time":"13:05","audioTime":785,"title":"A lull developed in the center","detail":"After Chalmers and Jackson moved toward Stuart, only Adams’s brigade faced the Wallace–Prentiss–Hurlbut line for most of the next hour."},{"time":"14:27","audioTime":867,"title":"Johnston believed the army was trapped","detail":"He thought the Confederate right had turned Grant’s left and that the rest of the United States army could be driven into the Owl and Snake Creek bottomlands."},{"time":"16:44","audioTime":1004,"title":"Appler heard the opening fighting","detail":"The 53rd Ohio formed after its pickets reported heavy firing, but Sherman again dismissed the warning."},{"time":"18:55","audioTime":1135,"title":"Cleburne’s brigade entered Ray Field","detail":"Its regiments crossed the southern end of the field while moving toward the United States camps."},{"time":"20:21","audioTime":1221,"title":"Sherman confirmed the attack","detail":"Confederate skirmishers fired at him from about 75 yards. Buckshot struck his right hand and killed his orderly, Thomas D. Holliday."},{"time":"22:49","audioTime":1369,"title":"The 53rd Ohio stopped the first assault","detail":"Appler’s regiment fired a close-range volley into two of Cleburne’s regiments and drove them back."},{"time":"24:30","audioTime":1470,"title":"Terrain divided Cleburne’s brigade","detail":"Mud and broken ground split the six-regiment line. Two regiments moved against Appler while four attacked Hildebrand and Buckland."},{"time":"26:21","audioTime":1581,"title":"Sherman stabilized his division","detail":"Although wounded and losing two horses, he directed Buckland and Hildebrand under sustained fire."},{"time":"28:52","audioTime":1732,"title":"Appler ordered a retreat","detail":"Several hundred men of the 53rd Ohio ran toward Pittsburg Landing. Other companies remained until their exposed flank forced them back."},{"time":"30:01","audioTime":1801,"title":"Raith reinforced Sherman’s left","detail":"Julius Raith brought four regiments from McClernand’s division and restored part of the line after the 53rd Ohio withdrew."},{"time":"31:59","audioTime":1919,"title":"Seven Confederate brigades faced Sherman and Raith","detail":"By about 9:30, formations from Hardee, Bragg, and Polk had converged around Shiloh Church without a single coordinating commander."},{"time":"33:36","audioTime":2016,"title":"Hildebrand’s brigade began to collapse","detail":"By about 10 a.m., the concentrated Confederate pressure had broken much of Sherman’s left after more than two hours of fighting."}],"command":[{"side":"United States","color":"#315f8c","branches":[{"commander":"Ulysses S. Grant","command":"Army of the Tennessee","subordinates":"Not yet on this part of the battlefield during the events covered"},{"commander":"William T. Sherman","command":"5th Division","subordinates":"Hildebrand, Buckland, and McDowell near Shiloh Church; Stuart detached near the river"},{"commander":"Jesse Hildebrand","command":"3rd Brigade, Sherman’s division","subordinates":"53rd, 57th, and 77th Ohio on Sherman’s left"},{"commander":"Ralph P. Buckland","command":"4th Brigade, Sherman’s division","subordinates":"Three Ohio regiments northwest of Shiloh Church"},{"commander":"Julius Raith","command":"Brigade, McClernand’s 1st Division","subordinates":"Four regiments reinforcing Sherman’s left"},{"commander":"W. H. L. Wallace","command":"2nd Division","subordinates":"Formed on Prentiss’s right and detached McArthur to Hurlbut"},{"commander":"Benjamin M. Prentiss","command":"Remnant of the 6th Division","subordinates":"Rallied survivors and the fresh 23rd Missouri along the farm lane"},{"commander":"Stephen A. Hurlbut","command":"4th Division","subordinates":"Two brigades on Prentiss’s left, extending through Bell Field"},{"commander":"David Stuart","command":"Detached brigade, Sherman’s division","subordinates":"Three regiments on the extreme United States left near the river"}]},{"side":"Confederacy","color":"#9a3d32","branches":[{"commander":"Albert Sidney Johnston","command":"Army of the Mississippi","subordinates":"Directed the front, diverted troops toward Stuart, and weakened the center"},{"commander":"P.G.T. Beauregard","command":"Rear headquarters","subordinates":"Sent additional formations toward the fighting around Shiloh Church"},{"commander":"Patrick Cleburne","command":"Brigade, Hardee’s corps","subordinates":"Six regiments; terrain split the line during attacks near Ray Field"},{"commander":"Patton Anderson","command":"Brigade, Bragg’s corps","subordinates":"Joined attacks against Sherman"},{"commander":"Bushrod Johnson / Robert Russell","command":"Brigades, Polk’s corps","subordinates":"Joined the concentration around Shiloh Church"},{"commander":"Sterling A. M. Wood","command":"Brigade, Hardee’s corps","subordinates":"Extended from the Prentiss sector into Ray Field"},{"commander":"James R. Chalmers / John K. Jackson","command":"Brigades on the Confederate right","subordinates":"Diverted toward Stuart after Lockett’s report"}]}],"people":[{"name":"William T. Sherman","role":"Misread the warning signs before the battle, then organized the defense around Shiloh Church after being wounded","side":"United States","image":"/images/william-t-sherman.jpg","source":"https://www.loc.gov/pictures/item/2018670507/"},{"name":"Jesse Appler","role":"Alerted his regiment before Sherman accepted that a general attack was underway, then ordered a premature retreat","side":"United States"},{"name":"Ephraim C. Dawes","role":"Adjutant of the 53rd Ohio who helped part of the regiment remain in line after Appler withdrew","side":"United States"},{"name":"Julius Raith","role":"Brought four regiments from McClernand’s division to reinforce Sherman’s exposed left","side":"United States"},{"name":"W. H. L. Wallace","role":"Commanded the 2nd Division and helped form the new United States center","side":"United States"},{"name":"Stephen A. Hurlbut","role":"Placed two brigades across Bell Field on the left of Prentiss","side":"United States"},{"name":"David Stuart","role":"Commanded the isolated brigade that Confederate scouts mistook for a full division","side":"United States"},{"name":"Albert Sidney Johnston","role":"Diverted forces toward Stuart and believed the United States army was nearly trapped","side":"Confederacy","image":"/images/albert-sidney-johnston.jpg","source":"https://www.loc.gov/pictures/item/2018670318/"},{"name":"Patrick Cleburne","role":"Led the six-regiment brigade attacking Sherman near Ray Field and Shiloh Church","side":"Confederacy"},{"name":"Samuel H. Lockett","role":"Reported Stuart’s brigade as a United States division advancing near the river","side":"Confederacy"}],"losses":[{"name":"Major General William T. Sherman","side":"United States","role":"Commander, 5th Division","outcome":"Wounded in the right hand by buckshot near Ray Field; remained in command and continued directing the defense"}],"gallery":[{"image":"/images/shiloh-battlefield-april-9.jpg","alt":"The Shiloh battlefield photographed April 9, 1862","caption":"Woods, ravines, and muddy low ground broke up long formations and separated adjacent units.","source":"https://www.loc.gov/pictures/item/2017646904/"},{"image":"/images/shiloh-battle-print.jpg","alt":"Historical print of the Battle of Shiloh","caption":"Sherman’s division and its reinforcements fought repeated close-range attacks around their camps.","source":"https://www.loc.gov/pictures/item/2018757088/"},{"image":"/images/pittsburg-landing-1862.jpg","alt":"Pittsburg Landing in 1862","caption":"Many routed soldiers gathered below the bluff at Pittsburg Landing, but the new center still covered the river base.","source":"https://www.loc.gov/pictures/item/2004660985/"}],"sources":[{"label":"Civil War Podcast episode 115","url":"https://civilwarpodcast.libsyn.com/115-shiloh-part-the-fifth"},{"label":"National Park Service: Battle of Shiloh","url":"https://www.nps.gov/shil/learn/historyculture/shiloh-history.htm"},{"label":"National Park Service: Shiloh maps","url":"https://www.nps.gov/shil/planyourvisit/maps.htm"},{"label":"Library of Congress: Shiloh battlefield map","url":"https://www.loc.gov/item/85690890/"},{"label":"Library of Congress: Shiloh battlefield photograph","url":"https://www.loc.gov/pictures/item/2017646904/"}]}}]}]
